<title>UK: Lloyds Bank sets $250 mln one-year bond.</title>
<headline>Lloyds Bank sets $250 mln one-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by lead manager Lehman Brothes.</p>
<p> BORROWER   LLOYDS TSB GROUP</p>
<p> AMT    $250 MLN	COUPON     6.0	 MATURITY    16.JUN.98</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  99.97     PAY DATE    16.JUN.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  10 BP     REOFFER    99.97     SPREAD	+22 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	AA2	 LISTING    LONDON    PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  =	   DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS US/UK</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  UK	  TAX PROVS   STD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    2.5 BP    SELL CONC  7.5 BP    PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND ONE YEAR U.S T-BILL</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED OFF EMTN PROGRAMME</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
